From e3753ce8d768711144543d8c7e4402e3cff13e75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:12:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: the scene's brightness from the game, where there is
 depth and above the sea

aurora_set_exposure(gain) brightens the scene after the HD look's effects and
before its bloom: kBoost, scene * (1 + gain - 1), where there is depth and
nothing up to 40 units above the sea's height, fully from 80. BlueWake sends
Wind Waker HD's own factor for the hour's palettes (its sunlight 3 times at
noon on actors and scenery, twice in the morning and evening, 1.65 and 1.37
after gamma). Off (0 or 1) the pass is left out. The gain rides in the pass's
copy of the view's seconds, which it doesn't read.

HD brightens the sun's light, not the sea: one gain over the whole scene
washed the sea out to a pale cyan before the deck was bright enough, and over
the sky it took the floating clouds to a clipped white.

Arch (Vulkan), Windfall's dock from the stage select with HD's palettes,
against Wind Waker HD in Cemu, 23 times from 4:00 to midnight: the deck,
cliffs and sea within about 10% of HD's at most hours (noon's deck 203,160,99
against 217,173,96, the sea 9,148,240 against 0,140,227).
